{"id":"mahabharata-1-026","work":"mahabharata","part":1,"partName":"आदिपर्व","partNameEn":"Adi Parva","unit":26,"title":"षड्विंशतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 26 · Garuda saves the Valakhilyas","summary":{"en":"Seeing the tiny Valakhilya sages hanging from the falling branch, Garuda holds it in his beak, and at Kashyapa's request they release it; he eats the elephant and tortoise on a mountain peak. In heaven terrible omens appear, Brihaspati tells Indra that Garuda is coming for the elixir, and the gods arm themselves.","kn":"ಮುರಿದ ಕೊಂಬೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ತೂಗುತ್ತಿದ್ದ ವಾಲಖಿಲ್ಯ ಋಷಿಗಳನ್ನು ಕಂಡು ಗರುಡನು ಅದನ್ನು ಕೊಕ್ಕಿನಲ್ಲಿ ಹಿಡಿಯುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಕಶ್ಯಪನ ಕೋರಿಕೆಯಂತೆ ಅವರು ಅದನ್ನು ಬಿಡುತ್ತಾರೆ, ಅವನು ಪರ್ವತಶಿಖರದಲ್ಲಿ ಆನೆ ಆಮೆಗಳನ್ನು ತಿನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಸ್ವರ್ಗದಲ್ಲಿ ಭೀಕರ ಅಪಶಕುನಗಳು ಕಾಣುತ್ತವೆ; ಗರುಡನು ಅಮೃತಕ್ಕಾಗಿ ಬರುತ್ತಿದ್ದಾನೆಂದು ಬೃಹಸ್ಪತಿ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ, ದೇವತೆಗಳು ಶಸ್ತ್ರಸಜ್ಜಿತರಾಗುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"गिरती शाखा से लटके नन्हे वालखिल्य ऋषियों को देखकर गरुड़ उसे चोंच में थाम लेते हैं; कश्यप के कहने पर ऋषि उसे छोड़ते हैं, और गरुड़ पर्वत-शिखर पर हाथी और कछुए को खाते हैं। स्वर्ग में भयानक अपशकुन होते हैं, बृहस्पति बताते हैं कि गरुड़ अमृत के लिए आ रहे हैं, और देवता शस्त्र उठाते हैं।","te":"విరిగిన కొమ్మకు వేలాడుతున్న వాలఖిల్య ఋషులను చూసి గరుడుడు దానిని ముక్కుతో పట్టుకుంటాడు; కశ్యపుని కోరికపై వారు దానిని వదులుతారు, అతడు పర్వతశిఖరంపై ఏనుగు తాబేళ్లను తింటాడు. స్వర్గంలో భయంకర అపశకునాలు కనిపిస్తాయి; గరుడుడు అమృతం కోసం వస్తున్నాడని బృహస్పతి చెబుతాడు, దేవతలు ఆయుధాలు ధరిస్తారు.","ta":"முறிந்த கிளையில் தொங்கும் சிறிய வாலகில்ய முனிவர்களைக் கண்டு கருடன் அதை அலகால் பற்றுகிறான்; கஶ்யபரின் வேண்டுகோளால் அவர்கள் அதை விட, அவன் மலைச் சிகரத்தில் யானையையும் ஆமையையும் உண்கிறான். ஸ்வர்க்கத்தில் கொடிய அபசகுனங்கள் தோன்ற, கருடன் அமுதத்துக்காக வருகிறான் என்று ப்ருஹஸ்பதி சொல்கிறார், தேவர்கள் ஆயுதம் ஏந்துகிறார்கள்.","ml":"വീണുകൊണ്ടിരുന്ന ശാഖയിൽ തൂങ്ങിക്കിടക്കുന്ന ചെറിയ വാലഖില്യ ഋഷിമാരെ കണ്ട ഗരുഡൻ, ശാഖ ചുണ്ടിൽ പിടിക്കുന്നു; കശ്യപന്റെ അപേക്ഷപ്രകാരം അവർ അതിനെ മോചിപ്പിക്കുന്നു. പിന്നെ ഒരു പർവതശിഖരത്തിലിരുന്ന് ആനയെയും ആമയെയും ഭക്ഷിക്കുന്നു. സ്വർഗത്തിൽ ഭയങ്കര ദുശ്ശകുനങ്ങൾ കാണുന്നു; ഗരുഡൻ അമൃത് തേടി വരുന്നുവെന്ന് ബൃഹസ്പതി ഇന്ദ്രനെ അറിയിക്കുന്നു, ദേവന്മാർ ആയുധമെടുക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 1.26; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Aug 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"आस्तीकपर्व","titleEn":"Astika Parva","verses":[{"text":"सूत उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Suta's son said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"स्पृष्टमात्रा तु पद्भ्यां सा गरुडेन बलीयसा ।\nअभज्यत तरोः शाखा भग्नां चैनामधारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The branch of the tree, barely touched by mighty Garuda's feet, snapped, and he held the broken branch."}},{"n":2,"text":"तां भग्नां स महाशाखां स्मयन्समवलोकयन् ।\nअथात्र लम्बतोऽपश्यद्वालखिल्यानधोमुखान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Smiling, he looked at the great broken branch, and then saw the Valakhilyas hanging from it head downward."}},{"n":3,"text":"स तद्विनाशसंत्रासादनुपत्य खगाधिपः ।\nशाखामास्येन जग्राह तेषामेवान्ववेक्षया ।\nशनैः पर्यपतत्पक्षी पर्वतान्प्रविशातयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fearing their destruction, the king of birds came down, and seized the branch in his beak, keeping his eyes on them, and flew slowly, shattering mountains as he went."}},{"n":4,"text":"एवं सोऽभ्यपतद्देशान्बहून्सगजकच्छपः ।\nदयार्थं वालखिल्यानां न च स्थानमविन्दत ॥","meaning":{"en":"So he passed over many lands with the elephant and tortoise, out of compassion for the Valakhilyas, finding no place to land."}},{"n":5,"text":"स गत्वा पर्वतश्रेष्ठं गन्धमादनमव्ययम् ।\nददर्श कश्यपं तत्र पितरं तपसि स्थितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He went to the best of mountains, the imperishable Gandhamadana, and saw his father Kashyapa there engaged in austerity."}},{"n":6,"text":"ददर्श तं पिता चापि दिव्यरूपं विहंगमम् ।\nतेजोवीर्यबलोपेतं मनोमारुतरंहसम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"His father saw the divine bird, endowed with brilliance, valor and strength, swift as mind and wind."}},{"n":7,"text":"शैलशृङ्गप्रतीकाशं ब्रह्मदण्डमिवोद्यतम् ।\nअचिन्त्यमनभिज्ञेयं सर्वभूतभयंकरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He looked like a mountain peak, like an uplifted rod of Brahma, unthinkable and unknowable, a terror to all beings."}},{"n":8,"text":"मायावीर्यधरं साक्षादग्निमिद्धमिवोद्यतम् ।\nअप्रधृष्यमजेयं च देवदानवराक्षसैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He bore magical power, like blazing fire in person, unassailable and unconquerable by gods, danavas and rakshasas."}},{"n":9,"text":"भेत्तारं गिरिशृङ्गाणां नदीजलविशोषणम् ।\nलोकसंलोडनं घोरं कृतान्तसमदर्शनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He could split mountain peaks and dry up rivers, shake the worlds, and was dreadful, like Death himself in appearance."}},{"n":10,"text":"तमागतमभिप्रेक्ष्य भगवान्कश्यपस्तदा ।\nविदित्वा चास्य संकल्पमिदं वचनमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him come, the blessed Kashyapa understood his purpose and spoke these words."}},{"n":11,"text":"पुत्र मा साहसं कार्षीर्मा सद्यो लप्स्यसे व्यथाम् ।\nमा त्वा दहेयुः संक्रुद्धा वालखिल्या मरीचिपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Son, do not act rashly, or you will be hurt at once. Do not let the angry Valakhilyas, who live on sunbeams, burn you.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"प्रसादयामास स तान्कश्यपः पुत्रकारणात् ।\nवालखिल्यांस्तपःसिद्धानिदमुद्दिश्य कारणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For his son's sake Kashyapa then appeased the Valakhilyas, perfected in austerity, giving this reason:"}},{"n":13,"text":"प्रजाहितार्थमारम्भो गरुडस्य तपोधनाः ।\nचिकीर्षति महत्कर्म तदनुज्ञातुमर्हथ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Ascetics, Garuda has begun this great deed for the good of creatures. He wishes to do it, and you should permit it.\""}},{"n":14,"text":"एवमुक्ता भगवता मुनयस्ते समभ्ययुः ।\nमुक्त्वा शाखां गिरिं पुण्यं हिमवन्तं तपोर्थिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed by the blessed one, those sages let go of the branch and went off to the holy Himalaya mountain, seeking austerity."}},{"n":15,"text":"ततस्तेष्वपयातेषु पितरं विनतात्मजः ।\nशाखाव्याक्षिप्तवदनः पर्यपृच्छत कश्यपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When they had gone, Vinata's son, his mouth still holding the branch, asked his father Kashyapa:"}},{"n":16,"text":"भगवन्क्व विमुञ्चामि तरुशाखामिमामहम् ।\nवर्जितं ब्राह्मणैर्देशमाख्यातु भगवान्मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Venerable one, where should I put down this branch? Tell me a place that brahmins avoid.\""}},{"n":17,"text":"ततो निष्पुरुषं शैलं हिमसंरुद्धकन्दरम् ।\nअगम्यं मनसाप्यन्यैस्तस्याचख्यौ स कश्यपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Kashyapa described a mountain with no people on it, its caves blocked with snow, that others could not reach even in thought."}},{"n":18,"text":"तं पर्वतमहाकुक्षिमाविश्य मनसा खगः ।\nजवेनाभ्यपतत्तार्क्ष्यः सशाखागजकच्छपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Entering in mind that mountain's great hollow, the bird Garuda flew swiftly there with the branch, the elephant and the tortoise."}},{"n":19,"text":"न तां वध्रः परिणहेच्छतचर्मा महानणुः ।\nशाखिनो महतीं शाखां यां प्रगृह्य ययौ खगः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Not even a strap of a hundred hides could have encircled the great branch of that tree, which the bird held as he flew."}},{"n":20,"text":"ततः स शतसाहस्रं योजनान्तरमागतः ।\nकालेन नातिमहता गरुडः पततां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In a short time the best of fliers had crossed a hundred thousand yojanas."}},{"n":21,"text":"स तं गत्वा क्षणेनैव पर्वतं वचनात्पितुः ।\nअमुञ्चन्महतीं शाखां सस्वनां तत्र खेचरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Instantly reaching that mountain as his father directed, the sky-goer dropped the great branch there with a crash."}},{"n":22,"text":"पक्षानिलहतश्चास्य प्राकम्पत स शैलराट् ।\nमुमोच पुष्पवर्षं च समागलितपादपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck by the wind of his wings, that king of mountains trembled and released a shower of flowers, its trees shaking loose."}},{"n":23,"text":"शृङ्गाणि च व्यशीर्यन्त गिरेस्तस्य समन्ततः ।\nमणिकाञ्चनचित्राणि शोभयन्ति महागिरिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The peaks of that mountain, variegated with jewels and gold, split apart on all sides, though they adorned the great mountain."}},{"n":24,"text":"शाखिनो बहवश्चापि शाखयाभिहतास्तया ।\nकाञ्चनैः कुसुमैर्भान्ति विद्युत्वन्त इवाम्बुदाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Many trees struck by that branch shone with golden blossoms, like clouds flickering with lightning."}},{"n":25,"text":"ते हेमविकचा भूयो युक्ताः पर्वतधातुभिः ।\nव्यराजञ्शाखिनस्तत्र सूर्यांशुप्रतिरञ्जिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those trees, gold-flowered and joined again with the mountain's minerals, shone, tinted by the rays of the sun."}},{"n":26,"text":"ततस्तस्य गिरेः शृङ्गमास्थाय स खगोत्तमः ।\nभक्षयामास गरुडस्तावुभौ गजकच्छपौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the best of birds settled on a peak of that mountain and ate both the elephant and the tortoise."}},{"n":27,"text":"ततः पर्वतकूटाग्रादुत्पपात मनोजवः ।\nप्रावर्तन्ताथ देवानामुत्पाता भयवेदिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he flew up swift as thought from the mountain's peak, and omens that reveal fear appeared to the gods."}},{"n":28,"text":"इन्द्रस्य वज्रं दयितं प्रजज्वाल व्यथान्वितम् ।\nसधूमा चापतत्सार्चिर्दिवोल्का नभसश्च्युता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Indra's beloved thunderbolt blazed in distress. A meteor with smoke and flames fell from the sky."}},{"n":29,"text":"तथा वसूनां रुद्राणामादित्यानां च सर्वशः ।\nसाध्यानां मरुतां चैव ये चान्ये देवतागणाः ।\nस्वं स्वं प्रहरणं तेषां परस्परमुपाद्रवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And the weapons of the Vasus, Rudras, Adityas, Sadhyas, Maruts and all other hosts of gods turned against one another."}},{"n":30,"text":"अभूतपूर्वं संग्रामे तदा देवासुरेऽपि च ।\nववुर्वाताः सनिर्घाताः पेतुरुल्काः समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There were such portents as never before, even in the wars of gods and asuras: winds blew with crashes, and meteors fell on every side."}},{"n":31,"text":"निरभ्रमपि चाकाशं प्रजगर्ज महास्वनम् ।\nदेवानामपि यो देवः सोऽप्यवर्षदसृक्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The cloudless sky rumbled loudly, and even the god of gods, Indra, rained blood."}},{"n":32,"text":"मम्लुर्माल्यानि देवानां शेमुस्तेजांसि चैव हि ।\nउत्पातमेघा रौद्राश्च ववर्षुः शोणितं बहु ।\nरजांसि मुकुटान्येषामुत्थितानि व्यधर्षयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The gods' garlands withered and their splendor faded. Dreadful omen-clouds rained much blood, and dust rose and fouled their crowns."}},{"n":33,"text":"ततस्त्राससमुद्विग्नः सह देवैः शतक्रतुः ।\nउत्पातान्दारुणान्पश्यन्नित्युवाच बृहस्पतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Indra, agitated with fear, saw these terrible omens and said to Brihaspati, together with the gods:"}},{"n":34,"text":"किमर्थं भगवन्घोरा महोत्पाताः समुत्थिताः ।\nन च शत्रुं प्रपश्यामि युधि यो नः प्रधर्षयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Venerable one, why have such dreadful omens arisen? I see no enemy in battle who could overpower us.\""}},{"text":"बृहस्पतिरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Brihaspati said:"}},{"n":35,"text":"तवापराधाद्देवेन्द्र प्रमादाच्च शतक्रतो ।\nतपसा वालखिल्यानां भूतमुत्पन्नमद्भुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Indra, through your fault and carelessness, a wondrous being has come into existence by the austerity of the Valakhilyas."}},{"n":36,"text":"कश्यपस्य मुनेः पुत्रो विनतायाश्च खेचरः ।\nहर्तुं सोममनुप्राप्तो बलवान्कामरूपवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is the son of the sage Kashyapa and Vinata, a bird who takes any form at will, mighty, who has come to carry off the soma."}},{"n":37,"text":"समर्थो बलिनां श्रेष्ठो हर्तुं सोमं विहंगमः ।\nसर्वं संभावयाम्यस्मिन्नसाध्यमपि साधयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That bird is able, the best of the strong, to seize the soma. I expect everything of him; he could accomplish even the impossible.\""}},{"text":"सूत उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Suta's son said:"}},{"n":38,"text":"श्रुत्वैतद्वचनं शक्रः प्रोवाचामृतरक्षिणः ।\nमहावीर्यबलः पक्षी हर्तुं सोममिहोद्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing this, Indra said to the guardians of the nectar: \"A bird of great valor and strength is trying to steal the soma here."}},{"n":39,"text":"युष्मान्संबोधयाम्येष यथा स न हरेद्बलात् ।\nअतुलं हि बलं तस्य बृहस्पतिरुवाच मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am warning you so that he cannot take it by force. Brihaspati has told me his strength is unmatched.\""}},{"n":40,"text":"तच्छ्रुत्वा विबुधा वाक्यं विस्मिता यत्नमास्थिताः ।\nपरिवार्यामृतं तस्थुर्वज्री चेन्द्रः शतक्रतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing this, the astonished gods made ready, and stood around the nectar, with Indra, wielder of the thunderbolt, of a hundred sacrifices."}},{"n":41,"text":"धारयन्तो महार्हाणि कवचानि मनस्विनः ।\nकाञ्चनानि विचित्राणि वैडूर्यविकृतानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"The resolute ones put on costly armor of gold, richly made and set with lapis lazuli."}},{"n":42,"text":"विविधानि च शस्त्राणि घोररूपाण्यनेकशः ।\nशिततीक्ष्णाग्रधाराणि समुद्यम्य सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They raised thousands of fearsome weapons of many kinds, with sharp and keen edges,"}},{"n":43,"text":"सविस्फुलिङ्गज्वालानि सधूमानि च सर्वशः ।\nचक्राणि परिघांश्चैव त्रिशूलानि परश्वधान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"flashing sparks and flames and smoke on every side: discuses, iron clubs, tridents and axes,"}},{"n":44,"text":"शक्तीश्च विविधास्तीक्ष्णाः करवालांश्च निर्मलान् ।\nस्वदेहरूपाण्यादाय गदाश्चोग्रप्रदर्शनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"and various sharp spears, bright swords and terrible maces, taking weapons that matched their own bodies in shape."}},{"n":45,"text":"तैः शस्त्रैर्भानुमद्भिस्ते दिव्याभरणभूषिताः ।\nभानुमन्तः सुरगणास्तस्थुर्विगतकल्मषाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With those gleaming weapons, adorned with divine ornaments, the radiant hosts of gods stood free of every stain."}},{"n":46,"text":"अनुपमबलवीर्यतेजसो\nधृतमनसः परिरक्षणेऽमृतस्य ।\nअसुरपुरविदारणाः सुरा\nज्वलनसमिद्धवपुःप्रकाशिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Of incomparable strength, valor and brilliance, and resolved to guard the nectar, those gods, who split the cities of asuras, shone with bodies lit like blazing fire."}},{"n":47,"text":"इति समरवरं सुरास्थितं\nपरिघसहस्रशतैः समाकुलम् ।\nविगलितमिव चाम्बरान्तरे\nतपनमरीचिविभासितं बभौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"So the gods stood in that excellent battlefield, crowded with hundreds of thousands of iron clubs, and it shone as if the sun, fallen from the sky, were lighting it with his rays."}}]}]}